@startuml ProximaDB Vector Lifecycle State Machine
!theme plain
title ProximaDB - Vector Record State Machine Diagram

[*] --> Incoming : insert request

state Incoming
Incoming : Validation pending
Incoming : ID assignment
Incoming : Timestamp setting

state InWAL
InWAL : Written to WAL
InWAL : In memory buffer
InWAL : Queryable
InWAL : Not yet in storage

state InMemtable
InMemtable : In LSM memtable
InMemtable : Fast access
InMemtable : Awaiting flush

state InStorage
InStorage : Flushed to disk
InStorage : In SSTable/Parquet
InStorage : Persistent

state Updated <<history>>
Updated : New version created
Updated : Old version marked
Updated : MVCC active

state Compacting
Compacting : Being reorganized
Compacting : Multiple versions
Compacting : Deduplication

state Expired
Expired : TTL exceeded
Expired : Marked for deletion
Expired : Still queryable

state Deleted
Deleted : Tombstone written
Deleted : Awaiting cleanup
Deleted : Not queryable

state Purged
Purged : Physically removed
Purged : Space reclaimed
Purged : No trace remains

Incoming --> InWAL : validation pass
Incoming --> [*] : validation fail

InWAL --> InMemtable : LSM path
InWAL --> InStorage : VIPER direct write
InWAL --> Updated : update request

InMemtable --> InStorage : memtable flush
InMemtable --> Updated : update request

InStorage --> Compacting : compaction triggered
InStorage --> Updated : update request
InStorage --> Expired : TTL reached
InStorage --> Deleted : delete request

Updated --> InWAL : new version
Updated --> Compacting : cleanup old versions

Compacting --> InStorage : compaction complete

Expired --> Deleted : cleanup cycle
Deleted --> Purged : compaction removes

Purged --> [*]

note right of InWAL
  WAL properties:
  - Sequence number
  - Write timestamp
  - Durability guarantee
end note

note left of Updated
  MVCC handling:
  - Keep latest version
  - Track version chain
  - Timestamp ordering
end note

note bottom of Compacting
  Compaction goals:
  - Remove duplicates
  - Merge small files
  - Apply TTL cleanup
  - Optimize layout
end note

@enduml